; The parent: signed, and vouched for by the trust anchor the scenario
; builds from the key clove generates for it.
;
; The delegation below carries NS and glue and no DS, which is what
; makes insecure.example. an insecure delegation: whatever it signs its
; data with, nothing here says a resolver should believe it.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.example.
ns		IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
www		IN	A	192.0.2.1
insecure	IN	NS	ns.insecure.example.
ns.insecure	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
